From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 020] panvk: gpu_prerast TLS descriptor, record IO, compute barrier
Generated-by: LLM

Purpose: Make the GPU prerast lowered VS actually execute and feed IDVS.
 - Lowered VS (RUN_COMPUTE) got TSD=0 (gfx.tsd is allocated later by
   prepare_draw) -> CS_FAULT DATA_INVALID_FAULT 0x58 on the COMPUTE group,
   no record store ran. Allocate a per-dispatch TLS descriptor via
   cmd_dispatch_prepare_tls and launch through cmd_dispatch_shader.
 - outputs_written/record_stride were read from info->nir before IO
   gathering (0) -> empty passthrough. Capture after panvk_lower_nir.
 - Passthrough: load_vertex_id (load_vertex_id_zero_base has no backend
   lowering -> SIGSEGV), per-slot output types, 16-bit outputs widened.
 - With gpu_prerast, COMPUTE subqueue is a consumer of DRAW_INDIRECT /
   vertex input / pre-raster stages so barriers wait before the dispatch.
Source/Reference: Mesa poly at 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (0xb8a31030, PAN_ARCH 11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b
Dependencies: csf, csf-v11/018
Validation test: tests/dxvk/vulkan/test_gpu_prerast_contracts.py, tests/dxvk/vulkan/gpu_prerast_slice.c

